ress resilience; and\u202f\u2022 understands complicated technology, reflecting solid technical and cognitive competence. Those strengths align closely with the core safety\u2011critical demands of a long\u2011distance pilot role.\nRegarding communication and adaptability:\n- **Communication** \u2013 Candidate\u202fC has difficulty communicating ideas, which is a noted weakness. Candidate\u202fB makes nasty remarks about colleagues, and Candidate\u202fA is regarded as a show\u2011off, both of which raise concerns about professional communication. Candidate\u202fD is seen as a know\u2011it\u2011all and has a hot temper, which can also affect crew interaction.\n- **Adaptability** \u2013 Candidate\u202fD responds to unexpected events adequately, showing good adaptability to changing situations. Candidate\u202fA is regarded as not open to new ideas, and Candidate\u202fC is not very willing to further his education, both indicating limited adaptability or feedback orientation. No specific adaptability observations were recorded for Candidate\u202fB."}
