{"id": 64, "ts": 1780433745.0386364, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s confirmation that Candidate\u202fC not only understands complex systems but also makes correct decisions quickly and stays calm in a crisis \u2013 exactly the technical competence and stress\u2011resilience we need for long\u2011distance flights. Those strengths reinforce my provisional vote for C.\u202fHowever, we must not overlook the concerns we already have: C is described as egocentric, has difficulty communicating ideas, and is not very willing to pursue further education. While he is 100\u202f% reliable and creates a positive crew atmosphere, poor communication can impair crew cooperation and professional interaction, which are essential for safety\u2011critical operations.\u202fGiven this trade\u2011off, I still favor Candidate\u202fC but would like to hear Emily\u2019s observations on how C\u2019s communication style translates into day\u2011to\u2011day crew cooperation, and whether D\u2019s arrogance and weak leadership might pose a greater risk in that regard."}
